    "doc_text": "AFP_ENG_19970422.0762\n\nTOKYO, April 23 , 1997 (AFP)\n\nNikkei up, dollar at 126.45-47 yen in Tokyo morning\n\n\n\n\nShare prices were higher on the Tokyo Stock Exchange Wednesday morning, but with profit-taking capping the upside, brokers said.\n\nThe Nikkei stock average rose 160.02 points, or 0.9 percent, to end the session at 18,704.47, down from a session high of 18,782.08.\n\nInvestors turned sellers among banks toward the end of the session and took profits on recent gains, brokers said.\n\n\"It is understandable to see such modest profit-taking among banks following their recent sustained gains,\" said a broker at New Japan Securities Co. Ltd.\n\nThe dollar was quoted at 126.45-47 yen in late morning trading, up from 126.32 yen in New York late Tuesday and from 126.02-05 yen here late Tuesday.",
